# Theme Runtime
- Theme state must support scoped providers and nested contexts.
- Do not assume a single global document/runtime when scoped runtime is possible.
- SSR must not require browser globals at module evaluation time.
- Runtime changes must be reactive and subscription-safe.
- Removing custom tokens must remove stale values.
- Parent theme values must not be treated as new local overrides.
- Theme Studio consumes Theme Runtime contracts; it is not a parallel implementation.
- Brand themes use tokens, not component forks.
